0:22Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5.1 Stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.1.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.1) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Metal (Forward+) - integrated Apple M1 Pro (Apple7) - Apple M1 Pro (8 threads) - 16.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nI've noticed that snapping objects to the grid does not work, for only one action, right after deleting an object using Cmd + Delete. The snapping tool remains on, but it does not work on the editor Gizmo.\n\nThis only happens for the next action I do, as the following action does work with snapping even if I use Undo to revert my previous action. Overall, it's more of a hassle than a big issue. \n\nI've noticed this happens with positioning, rotating, and even dragging objects from the Filesystem to the editor.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nDelete an object in the 3D editor.\nMove another object in the editor using the 3D Gizmo.\nThe object will move without snapping.\nThe next action will have snapping back on.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nI've noticed it happens in every instance of the 3D editor, in every project.\n\n[test.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23567314/test.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.